A||||8||fropuff||Belt question||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||06-21-2001||12:54 AM||||<BR>Hey there.  I have a problem with my belts, I think.  It occurs when the fan is on, whenever the A/C, defrost, etc. is on.  It comes from the engine compartment.  It sounds like a sqeaky-ass belt.  Very loud.  Occurs for a few seconds (10).  It's intermittent too.  Not always happens.  When I turn the fan controls to off, it quits.  What is this?  Fan belt?  If I get an underdrive pulley kit, will it be fixed?  Thanks a lot for any help.  I really appreciate it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||06-21-2001||01:29 AM||||Well, 1st off I would recommend inspecting your belts, and changing them if they are worn or cracked.  If they are ok, my bet would be that they are loose.  <P>To adjust the main pulley (Iam assuming it's a v-6) You need to loosen the alternator to adjust the tension.  To tighten the A/C belt, you need to loosen the A/C compressor to adjust the tension.  (not a fun job)<P>And yes, pullies would probably fix this, as long as there is proper tension on the belts.  <P>This squealing might be something more serious though if belt adjustment doesn't fix it.  Such as alternator, waterpump, or A/C compressor failure.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||06-21-2001||09:01 AM||||Originally posted by AkursedX:  <BR>"...This squealing might be something more serious though if belt adjustment doesn't fix it.  Such as alternator, waterpump, or A/C compressor failure."<P>&gt;Holy sh*t; I don't want that at all.  I'll try to see if the belt is bad or just loose.  Thanks again!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||06-21-2001||09:02 AM||||Originally posted by AkursedX:  <BR>"...This squealing might be something more serious though if belt adjustment doesn't fix it.  Such as alternator, waterpump, or A/C compressor failure."<P>&gt;Holy sh*t; I don't want that at all.  I'll try to see if the belt is bad or just loose.  Thanks again!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||06-21-2001||09:11 AM||||Replace them, trustr me on this one I had to constantly tighten my belts about once every 2 weeks until I ran out of adjustment. Ifinaly changed them and the problem went away.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SteveJ||06-21-2001||09:12 AM||||Yea I'd say you have a loose or worn belt, but there may be the underlying problem in the AC. Seems to me I've seen here on the board that if the charge is low the system cycles very fast like that. So every time it cycles you squeal. So turn it on so it makes the noise then go look at the compressor clutch and see if it engages in time with the noise.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||06-21-2001||11:45 PM||||Originally posted by SteveJ:<BR>"Seems to me I've seen here on the board that if the charge is low the system cycles very fast like that. So every time it cycles you squeal. So turn it on so it makes the noise then go look at the compressor clutch and see if it engages in time with the noise."<P>&gt;Actually, the noise does not always occur when I turn the A/C on.  Actually, it usually never does squeal when the A/C is turned on.  All it does is squeal intermittently, for like 5-10 seconds at a time.  It usually does it once, then it's done.<P>||||reg||1
